member.summary:
Helper struct to easily calculate statistics (execute count / min / max / avg / total time)

Usage:

    StatsHolder defined as field on a class (e.g.)

    Statsholder _s = new StatsHolder();

    Whenever executing the action you want to measure:

    DateTime start = DateTime.Now;
    ... do actions
    _s.Update(start);

    When timing needs to be listed

    string info = _s.ToString();

Parser for formatting strings used in protocols (to combine values and fixed text). Syntax: sometext{type:identifier}othertext{othertype}
Possible types: sessionVar, elementName, elementProperty, pid, extPid, rowPK, rowDK Curly braces can be escaped: \{ and \} \n, \t and \\ are replaced by a newline, a tab and '\' respectively.
An identifier can contain an escaped curly brace. If the identifier is empty, the ':' can be omitted.

Replaces the format items by {0}, {1}, etc.
Remaining curly braces will be escaped ('{' => '{{', '}' => '}}', '\{' => '{{', '\}' => '}}')
These escaped characters will be parsed: \{, \n, \t

Example:
{pid:1000}_escapedCurly\}__{sessionVar:var1}UnmatchedCurly:{
=>
{0}_escapedCurly}}__{1}UnmatchedCurly:{{

Use the resulting string, combine it with a List of values of the items returned by GetFormatItems and pass these two to String.Format
Ex: 
var format = new ProtocolStringFormatParser(protocolFormattingString);
return String.Format(format.GetStringFormatCompatibleString(), GetValues(format.GetFormatItems()).ToArray());

